      "body": "<h2>1. The Capstone Mission: Project Apex Scale</h2>\n<p>Apex Cloud Technologies is a fast-growing enterprise SaaS company that recently closed an $80 million Series C financing round. Currently at 115 employees across 3 US states, the executive board has mandated scaling headcount to <strong>1,000 employees across 12 countries and 35 US states over the next 24 months</strong>. Existing HR infrastructure consists of a disjointed patchwork: payroll run on basic QuickBooks, resumes tracked in Google Sheets, zero formal salary bands, outdated employee handbooks, and no performance review system.</p>\n<p>As the newly appointed <strong>Director of People Operations / Senior HR Generalist</strong>, you are tasked with architecting and executing the complete institutionalization of people operations (Project Apex Scale).</p>\n<h2>2. Capstone Deliverable Matrix</h2>\n<table class=\"comparison-table\">\n  <thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>Core Deliverable</th><th>Key Specifications & Content</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><strong>1. Job Architecture & Compensation</strong></td><td>Enterprise Leveling Matrix & Salary Bands</td><td>6 career levels (IC1 to IC6, M1 to M3); Hay evaluation factor grading; P50 market salary bands across 5 job families; compa-ratio modeling; 409A stock option allocation framework.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>2. Talent Acquisition Engine</strong></td><td>Full-Stack Hiring Architecture</td><td>Greenhouse ATS pipeline configuration; structured behavioral interview scorecards; STAR question banks; candidate experience SLAs; 30% Mansfield diverse sourcing slate mandate.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>3. Compliance & Policy Shield</strong></td><td>Multi-State Employee Handbook & FLSA Audit</td><td>Comprehensive handbook with prominent at-will disclaimers; California/New York statutory addenda; full FLSA exemption audit of all 65 job descriptions; EEO-1 reporting readiness.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>4. Performance & Total Rewards</strong></td><td>Continuous Performance Management System</td><td>Quarterly OKR framework; weekly 1-on-1 cadences; bi-annual calibration committee protocol; Safe Harbor 401(k) plan with 4% match; HDHP/PPO medical tier with triple-tax-advantaged HSA.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>5. HR Tech Ecosystem</strong></td><td>Global HRIS & Integration Architecture</td><td>Workday HCM master migration blueprint; SCIM automated provisioning to Okta; Deel EOR integration for 15 international entities; EDI 834 carrier feeds; RBAC data privacy matrix.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>6. Culture & Analytics</strong></td><td>People Intelligence Dashboard</td><td>Gallup Q12 annual survey; quarterly eNPS pulse; predictive flight risk scoring model; structured 30-60-90 day onboarding roadmap; executive HR scorecard.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>3. Synthesis: Transforming Talent into Enterprise Value</h2>\n<p>This capstone synthesizes all 28 preceding chapters. The student demonstrates end-to-end mastery across statutory labor compliance, compensation modeling, talent acquisition, human conflict mediation, systems integration, and organizational development, proving their readiness to lead People Operations in fast-scaling global enterprises.</p>"
